 ## Discord ops alerts
 
@@ -69,6 +69,8 @@ ## Discord ops alerts
 | Env | `DISCORD_WEBHOOK_URL` → `config('services.discord.webhook_url')` |
 | Client | `App\Ops\DiscordOpsAlert::send($title, $message, $context = [])` |
 | Unconfigured | Empty/missing URL → silent no-op (safe for CI) |
+| Mention | `DISCORD_MENTION_ID` → `config('services.discord.mention_id')`. Optional Discord user ID (17–20 digits, surrounding whitespace trimmed). When valid, every alert ends with `<@ID>` on its own line so the on-call person is pinged. Empty or invalid (`@everyone`, `abc`, `123`, values with newlines, …) → no mention, silently |
+| Length | Content is capped at 1800 characters **including** the mention; long title/message/context is truncated to make room for it |
 | Failures | Non-2xx / transport errors are logged without the webhook URL; they do not throw |
 
 Call from jobs/handlers when a notable ops event occurs; do not wire every exception globally.
